Modifications made in ProkBot Plus (2026-11-07 to 2026-11-12)
--------------------------------------------------------------

1. Windows x64 client (new)
   - windows/: patcher, Windows recipes ported from the macOS recipes,
     per-user installer source, prebuilt grokbot-tailcat.exe and installer
     stub, tests.
   - mac/clients/desktop/: cross-platform changes shared by the macOS and
     Windows clients (platform.mjs, main.mjs, connection.mjs, settings.mjs,
     sounds.mjs, connect.css, native-provider.mjs, codex-bridge.mjs,
     codex-process.mjs). Windows command output uses the original daemon's
     UTF-8 console option (local-exec.mjs). Host image paths are parsed with
     POSIX rules on Windows (attachments.mjs).
   - host/runtime/host-computers.mjs, native-desktop.mjs, codex-prompt.mjs,
     host/server/desktop-capabilities.mjs: the Host recognizes Windows
     computers.

2. Model API formats
   - New Anthropic Messages and OpenAI Responses adapters next to OpenAI Chat:
     host/runtime/anthropic-messages.mjs, openai-responses.mjs,
     openai-chat.mjs, model-common.mjs (new); model-session.mjs,
     model-policy.mjs, model-router.mjs, model-errors.mjs,
     model-observation.mjs, config.mjs, host/server/models.mjs, index.mjs,
     public/model.js, public/locales-en.js (changed).
   - "minimal" reasoning effort, reasoning provenance tags, optional-parameter
     fallback, connection test and auto review for all three formats.

3. Auto review: retry once on a malformed classification and log failures
   (host/runtime/host-auto-review.mjs).

4. Web and image tools
   - Native web tools fall back to automatic tool choice when a model rejects a
     forced tool call; parallel searches succeed when one call succeeds
     (host/runtime/web-services.mjs).
   - Aspect ratios are mapped to image sizes, and reference images use the
     image edits endpoint (host/server/media-providers.mjs, media-http.mjs,
     media-settings.mjs, host/runtime/media-services.mjs).

5. Message order: messages from one model response are delivered in the order
   the model wrote them (host/runtime/reliability/tool-order.mjs (new),
   tool-journal.mjs, host/runtime/model-common.mjs).

6. Linux deployment: host/release/build-docker.py accepts the image identity
   reported by Docker 29's containerd image store; host/network/build-tailcat.py
   builds the Windows target; Dockerfile.base and Dockerfile.execution set the
   executable bit on the Tailcat binary.

7. Admin command-line tool (new): host/tools/host-admin.mjs.

8. Tests: host/tests/ (new), windows/tests/ (new),
   mac/tests/desktop-external-links.test.mjs (locale-independent assertion).

9. Documentation: README, docs/AI-INSTALL, docs/ARCHITECTURE (now also covering
   the upstream DETAILS.md, TODO.md and install notes), module READMEs (host and
   ios now also cover the upstream DEPLOYMENT, PLUGINS and SIGNING notes),
   AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, GitHub issue and pull request
   templates. The unused file list host/source-files.json was removed.

10. Android client (new)
   - android/shell/: Android shell app (Kotlin, no third-party libraries):
     loopback gateway to the paired Host, Keystore-encrypted credential,
     pairing, background notifications, file picking and saving, back gesture.
     android/dist/grokbot-android-shell.apk is its prebuilt release build.
   - android/client/: bridge that runs the original desktop interface in the
     Android WebView in place of Electron's main process and preloads, the
     computer view frame, a phone layout after the official phone app (the
     Bot list and conversations as separate screens, round floating buttons,
     message bubbles, full-screen pages and bottom sheets), an anchor
     positioning fallback and the connection page.
   - android/patchers/: builds the APK from the user's own official Windows
     installer (ZIP writing, APK Signature Scheme v2 signing with a key created
     for the user) and applies a few verified changes to the original
     interface (renderer-patches.mjs).
   - windows/patchers/desktop/original.mjs: extraction of the official
     installer moved out of patch.mjs so the Android patcher can share it.
   - android/tests/ (new).

11. Client reliability and validation: installer ownership checks, verified
    Windows installer inputs and cleanup, Android gateway limits, attachment
    save and notification fixes, distinct mobile and Windows device labels,
    model redirect protection and reliable ordered-message timeouts. Added
    regression tests, an optional cross-platform CI template and Android
    emulator screenshots, including real Chinese and English conversations.

12. ARM64 Host build path, locked ARM runtime dependencies, ARM64 Tailcat,
    deployment platform checks, operator CLI and upgrade safeguards; revised
    bilingual installation and architecture guides, version-input checks and
    deployment regression coverage. Documented Oracle Ampere A1 runtime
    verification with a separate amd64 desktop. The original desktop is unchanged.

Public documentation correction (2026-11-14): clarified tested hardware,
Apple device coverage, version pins and volume-only backup scope. No official
program or changed release binary is included in that correction.

Client tools update (2026-11-14): separate Android app and renderer versions,
verify patched inputs in scratch, and publish independently checked client
tool archives. Official programs and generated clients are not distributed.
The server implementation is unchanged from the prior default branch.

Third-party components
----------------------

Third-party components keep their own licenses. See host/THIRD_PARTY,
mac/THIRD_PARTY, ios/THIRD_PARTY and mac/patchers/desktop/node_modules.
android/shell/gradle/wrapper/ contains the Gradle Wrapper, and the prebuilt
Android shell includes parts of the Kotlin standard library; both are
licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

Original Grok Bot programs
--------------------------

This repository contains no Grok Bot program files. The patch tools download
the official programs on the user's own machine, verify their hashes and patch
them there. Grok, Grok Bot and related names and marks belong to their
respective owners. ProkBot Plus is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.
